  <h1>Lesson 15: Flexbox in CSS</h1>
  <p>Learn How to Put Boxes Side by Side with display: flex, justify-content, align-items | LearnHTMLCSSJS.com</p>
</header>

<div class="container">
  <div class="tabs">
    <button id="lessonTabBtn" class="tab-btn active" onclick="showLesson()">📖 Lesson</button>
    <button id="testTabBtn" class="tab-btn" onclick="showTest()">📝 Test - 100 Marks</button>
  </div>
  <div id="lockMsg" class="lock-msg">🔒 Test is running! All tabs are locked until you submit the test or time ends.</div>

  <div id="lessonContent">
    <h2>1. What is Flexbox?</h2>
    <p><b>Flexbox</b> is used to <b>put boxes side by side</b> and control their alignment easily.</p>
    <p>Before Flexbox, developers had a very hard time putting 3 cards in one row. With Flexbox, it is just 1 line: <b>display: flex;</b></p>
    <div class="note"><b>Example:</b> 3 product cards in Daraz, 3 pricing plans, Navbar logo + menu - all are made with Flexbox.</div>
    <h2>2. Without Flexbox vs With Flexbox</h2>
    <div class="result"><b>Without Flexbox (Normal divs - One below other):</b><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center">Box 1</div><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center">Box 2</div><div style="background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:12px;border-radius:8px;margin:6px 0;text-align:center">Box 3</div></div>
    <div class="result" style="margin-top:12px"><b>With Flexbox (display: flex; - Side by Side):</b><div class="flex-demo"><div class="flex-item">Box 1</div><div class="flex-item2">Box 2</div><div class="flex-item3">Box 3</div></div></div>
    <h2>3. Basic Flexbox - Only 2 Lines</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">&lt;!-- HTML --&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"container"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"box"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Box 1</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"box"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Box 2</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="tag">&lt;div</span> <span class="attr">class</span>=<span class="val">"box"</span><span class="tag">&gt;</span><span class="text">Box 3</span><span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br>
<span class="tag">&lt;/div&gt;</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* CSS - Only this one line makes magic */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Gap between boxes */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">.box</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">flex</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">1</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* All boxes equal width */</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="note"><b>Important Rule:</b> <b>display: flex;</b> is always written on the <b>PARENT</b> (container), not on the child boxes.</div>
    <h2>4. justify-content - Left, Center, Right, Space Between</h2>
    <p><b>justify-content</b> controls alignment <b>horizontally</b> (Left to Right).</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      <tr><td>flex-start</td><td>All boxes on Left (Default)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>center</td><td>All boxes in Center</td></tr>
      <tr><td>flex-end</td><td>All boxes on Right</td></tr>
      <tr><td>space-between</td><td>First box Left, Last box Right, Equal gap</td></tr>
      <tr><td>space-around</td><td>Equal space around each box</td></tr>
      <tr><td>space-evenly</td><td>Equal space everywhere</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">justify-content</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">space-between</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Most used for Navbar */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><p style="margin:0 0 5px"><b>justify-content: flex-start; (Left)</b></p><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;background:#f1f5f9;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">1</div><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">2</div></div><p style="margin:10px 0 5px"><b>justify-content: center;</b></p><div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;gap:10px;background:#f1f5f9;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">1</div><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">2</div></div><p style="margin:10px 0 5px"><b>justify-content: space-between; (Navbar Style)</b></p><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;background:#f1f5f9;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">Logo</div><div style="background:#f59e0b;color:white;padding:10px 15px;border-radius:6px">Menu</div></div></div>
    <h2>5. align-items - Top, Center, Bottom</h2>
    <p><b>align-items</b> controls alignment <b>vertically</b> (Top to Bottom).</p>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Value</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
      <tr><td>flex-start</td><td>Top</td></tr>
      <tr><td>center</td><td>Middle - Most Used</td></tr>
      <tr><td>flex-end</td><td>Bottom</td></tr>
      <tr><td>stretch</td><td>Full height (Default)</td></tr>
    </table>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Center anything - Perfect Center Trick */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">justify-content</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Horizontal Center */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">align-items</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Vertical Center */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">height</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">200px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Perfect Center:</b><div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;align-items:center;height:120px;background:#e0f2fe;border-radius:10px"><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:15px 25px;border-radius:8px;font-weight:bold">I am in Perfect Center!</div></div></div>
    <h2>6. flex-direction - Row or Column</h2>
    <p><b>flex-direction</b> controls direction - Row (side by side) or Column (one below other).</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">flex-direction</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">row</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Side by side - Default */</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">flex-direction</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">column</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* One below other */</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result:</b><p style="margin:0 0 5px"><b>flex-direction: row;</b></p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:row;gap:10px;background:#f1f5f9;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;flex:1;text-align:center">1</div><div style="background:#2563eb;color:white;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;flex:1;text-align:center">2</div></div><p style="margin:10px 0 5px"><b>flex-direction: column;</b></p><div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#f1f5f9;padding:10px;border-radius:8px"><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;text-align:center">1</div><div style="background:#16a34a;color:white;padding:10px;border-radius:6px;text-align:center">2</div></div></div>
    <h2>7. flex-wrap - If Boxes Don't Fit</h2>
    <p>If you have 6 boxes and screen is small, boxes will get squeezed. <b>flex-wrap: wrap;</b> moves extra boxes to the next line.</p>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="tag">.container</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">flex-wrap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">wrap</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <h2>8. Full Example - 3 Cards + Navbar</h2>
    <div class="code-box"><code>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* Navbar */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.navbar</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">justify-content</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">space-between</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">align-items</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">center</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br><br>
<span class="comment" style="color:#94a3b8">/* 3 Cards */</span><br>
<span class="tag">.cards</span> <span class="text">{</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">display</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">flex</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;<span class="attr">gap</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">15px</span><span class="text">;</span><br>
<span class="text">}</span><br>
<span class="tag">.card</span> <span class="text">{</span> <span class="attr">flex</span><span class="text">:</span> <span class="val">1</span><span class="text">;</span> <span class="text">}</span>
    </code></div>
    <div class="result"><b>Result - Navbar + 3 Cards:</b><div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;background:#0f172a;color:white;padding:12px 15px;border-radius:8px;margin-bottom:10px"><b>My Website</b><span>Home | About | Contact</span></div><div style="display:flex;gap:12px"><div style="flex:1;background:white;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center"><b>Card 1</b><br><span style="color:#64748b">HTML</span></div><div style="flex:1;background:white;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center"><b>Card 2</b><br><span style="color:#64748b">CSS</span></div><div style="flex:1;background:white;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;padding:15px;border-radius:10px;text-align:center"><b>Card 3</b><br><span style="color:#64748b">JS</span></div></div></div>
    <h2>9. Homework - Practice for 2 Minutes</h2>
    <p>In Playground, make this:</p>
    <p>1. One <b>Navbar</b> - display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;<br>2. One <b>div class="cards"</b> - display: flex; gap: 15px; with 3 cards inside, each flex: 1;<br>3. One <b>Center Box</b> - display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; height: 200px;</p>
    <div class="box"><b>Remember:</b> Flexbox = Side by Side | display: flex; = On PARENT | gap = Gap between boxes | flex: 1; = Equal width | justify-content = Horizontal (Left / Center / space-between) | align-items = Vertical (Top / Center / Bottom) | flex-direction = row / column | flex-wrap: wrap; = Next line if no space</div>
    <p><b>Next Step:</b> After this lesson, go to <a href="/lesson16">Lesson 16 - Grid Layout</a> to learn Grid - Flexbox's bigger brother for full page layouts.</p>
    <a id="playgroundLink" class="btn" href="/playground">▶ Try it Yourself - Playground</a><br><br>
    <button class="btn btn-next" onclick="showTest()">Go to Test → 📝</button>
    <div class="nav">
      <a class="btn btn-prev" href="/lesson14">← Lesson 14</a>
      <a id="nextLessonLink" class="btn btn-next" href="/lesson16">Next Lesson 16 →</a>
    </div>
  </div>

