          <div class="question"><b>Q1. Flexbox is used for?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="a"> Put boxes side by side</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="b"> Change text color</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="c"> Make images</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="d"> Make database</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q2. display: flex; is written on?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="a"> PARENT (Container)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="b"> CHILD (Box)</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="c"> Body only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="d"> Head only</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q3. Which controls Horizontal alignment?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="a"> justify-content</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="b"> align-items</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="c"> flex-direction</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="d"> gap</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q4. Which controls Vertical alignment?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="a"> justify-content</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="b"> align-items</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="c"> flex-direction</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="d"> flex-wrap</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q5. Which value puts First box Left and Last box Right?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="a"> justify-content: space-between;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="b"> justify-content: center;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="c"> justify-content: flex-start;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q5" value="d"> justify-content: flex-end;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q6. Which makes all boxes Equal Width?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="a"> flex: 1;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="b"> gap: 1;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="c"> flex: 0;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q6" value="d"> width: 1;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q7. Which property creates Gap between boxes?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="a"> gap</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="b"> margin only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="c"> padding only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q7" value="d"> border</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q8. Which moves extra boxes to Next Line?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="a"> flex-wrap: wrap;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="b"> flex-wrap: nowrap;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="c"> flex-direction: row;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q8" value="d"> gap: wrap;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q9. Which makes boxes One Below Other?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="a"> flex-direction: column;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="b"> flex-direction: row;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="c"> display: block;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q9" value="d"> flex-wrap: wrap;</label></div>
          <div class="question"><b>Q10. To Perfectly Center a box, you need?</b><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="a"> display: flex; + justify-content: center; + align-items: center;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="b"> display: flex; only</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="c"> gap: center;</label><label><input type="radio" name="q10" value="d"> margin: center;</label></div>
